        type: "single",
        question: "**Task 3 **\n**Young Explorers **\n**Charlie Smith**\nAt 20 years old, expedition leader Charlie Smith was the youngest person to have crossed Iceland from north to south unsupported. Charlie was also part of the Coldest Crossing team who attempted to complete the first mid-winter, unsupported crossing of Iceland on an 18-day, 250-mile journey. However, the attempt went wrong. Soon after starting their journey, one of the hikers was flown back to Britain as he was suffering from a bad infection. A second from the team suffered frostbite to his toes and had to return. The rest of the group were rescued by the helicopter in the approaching storm.\n**This explorer ___________________.**",
