        id: "eng-557-16",
        type: "single",
        question: "**Most Unusual Towns in the World**\n**Longyearbyen, Norway**\nThe town of Longyearbyen is the world’s northernmost city. The name of the town is literal, actually meaning “long year.” The sun sets each year on October 25th and does not rise again for four months. The citizens are used to living alongside polar bears and reindeer. It’s home to the world’s northernmost gourmet restaurant, the historic Huset, which boasts one of Europe’s largest wine cellars. But perhaps the most interesting thing about Longyearbyen is that its citizens aren’t allowed to die. There is a cemetery in the town, but it hasn’t been used for 70 years.\n**Which town ________________________?**",
