        id: "eng-394-27",
        type: "single",
        question: "**Edinburgh Castle**\nLocated on an extinct volcano is the powerful Scottish symbol of Edinburgh Castle. It captivates visitors with so much to see in its ancient buildings and panoramic views of the city. See the room where the future King James, son of Mary, Queen of Scots, was born, or the Honours of Scotland, also known as the Scottish Crown Jewels, which are among the oldest in Europe, and the Stone of Destiny, the ancient coronation seat of Scotland’s Kings. Witness the firing of the One o’clock gun which has become an Edinburgh tradition since 1861.\n**Which of the places _____________?**",
