        id: "eng-64-5",
        type: "single",
        question: "**Read the texts below. Match choices (A–H) to (1–5). There are three choices you do not need to use.**\nBy sticking out their tongues, people react to situations that may be unpleasant for them. Such displays indicate laughing or rejection. For example, children often stick out their tongues to tease each other. Or, they may also stick out their tongues in reaction to activities requiring close concentration; hence, the tongue-showing of children focused on their homework.",
